      \field{abstract}{Europe is at a make-or-break moment in the global AI race, squeezed between the massive venture capital and tech giants in the US and China’s scale-oriented, top-down drive. At this tipping point, where the convergence of AI with complementary and synergistic technologies, like quantum computing, biotech, VR/AR, 5G/6G, robotics, advanced materials, and high-performance computing, could upend geopolitical balances, Europe needs to rethink its AI-related strategy. On the heels of the AI Action Summit 2025 in Paris, we present a sharp, doable strategy that builds upon Europe’s strengths and closes gaps.}
